    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW21kRXq9R8f9BL3eSYVrQpsh)_\n\n- `sp-org-tag-groups` binds `M-o n i` to `sp-insert-note` in `org-mode-map`, next to `M-o n a` (`vulpea-buffer-alias-add`). The old `M-o n i` of the removed `org-node` module is gone.\n- New `sp-find-note`: `vulpea-find` run with the tag emoji and the coloured tag column (same wrapper as `sp-insert-note`); takes the keywords of `vulpea-find`. Bound globally to `M-o f`.\n- The `M-o f` binding of `vulpea-find` is removed from `sp-vulpea-base`, so load order cannot decide which one wins.\n- `sp-select-note` is a function other commands call, not a command, so it has no key.\n- Docs and `.el` edited together (`sp-org-tag-groups.org`, `sp-vulpea.org`).\n\nNot run in Emacs (none in the container); `sp-find-note` assumes `vulpea-find` picks its notes with `vulpea-select-from`, so the emoji and column apply through the let-bound options, as they do for `vulpea-insert`. No CHANGELOG edits.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNi9sdrKxJ3CH27TGGqB",
